/T (consumption correctly.Since meter readings are non-negative, an unsigned integer is appropriate for storingthem.During normal operation, consumption is calculated by subtracting the previousreading from the current reading. When the meter reaches its maximum reading androlls over to zero, the program uses the full meter range of 65,536 to calculate the unitsconsumed.For example, the normal readings of 1200 and 1530 produce 330 units. Intherollover example, a previous reading of 65400 and a current reading of 120 produce256 units. Input validation prevents readings outside the permitted range from being accepted. )
