<<
/Title (If the program is split into input.c, tariff.c and report.c with a shared header, each source file is compiled separately into an object file and then linked. After changing only tariff.c, only tariff.c normally needs recompilation; the other object files can be reused, followed by relinking. In a single-file build, changing the file requires recompiling the whole translation unit. Separate compilation reduces rebuild time for larger projects, but object files require additional disk space. The total object-file space is approximately the sum of the object sizes.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
